---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Non-Profit Mailing Guide & PS Form 3624 | Cornerstone Services"
  description="Complete guide to USPS non-profit mailing rates, PS Form 3624 application, eligibility requirements, and how to save 40-60% on postage for your 501(c)(3) organization."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Non-Profit Mailing Guide"
    subtitle="Everything your 501(c)(3) needs to know about discounted USPS non-profit postage rates and the PS Form 3624 application."
    breadcrumbs={[
      { label: 'Direct Mail Tools', href: '/direct-mail-tools/' },
      { label: 'Non-Profit Mailing' },
    ]}
  />
  <!-- FAQPage Schema -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'What is PS Form 3624?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'PS Form 3624 is the USPS application form that non-profit organizations must submit to qualify for discounted non-profit mailing rates. It requires documentation of your 501(c)(3) status and organizational purpose.' },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'How much can non-profits save on postage?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Qualifying non-profits typically save 40-60% compared to commercial mailing rates. For example, a Marketing Mail letter that costs approximately $0.247 at automation rates may cost as little as $0.146 at non-profit automation rates.' },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'What organizations qualify for non-profit mailing rates?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Eligible organizations include 501(c)(3) charities, religious organizations, educational institutions, scientific organizations, veterans groups, fraternal organizations, and qualifying political committees.' },
      },
    ],
  })} />
  <section class="py-14 lg:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="section-divider mb-6"></div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-display text-crst-primary mb-6">
          Save 40–60% on Postage with Non-Profit Rates
        </h2>
        <p class="text-navy-600/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          If your organization has 501(c)(3) tax-exempt status, you may qualify for dramatically reduced USPS <a href="/direct-mail-tools/postage-rates/" class="text-crst-primary underline hover:text-crst-gold">postage rates</a>. Non-profit Marketing Mail rates are among the lowest postage rates available — often saving organizations thousands of dollars per year on fundraising appeals, newsletters, event invitations, and <a href="/direct-mail-marketing/" class="text-crst-primary underline hover:text-crst-gold">direct mail campaigns</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="text-navy-600/80 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Cornerstone has helped dozens of non-profit organizations across the Hudson Valley apply for and maintain their USPS non-profit mailing authorization. We guide you through the PS Form 3624 application, handle all presort processing, and ensure every mailing meets USPS requirements for non-profit pricing.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-display text-crst-primary mb-4">Non-Profit vs. Commercial Rate Comparison</h3>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-10">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="bg-crst-primary text-white">
                <th class="text-left p-3 rounded-tl-lg">Mail Type</th>
                <th class="text-right p-3">Commercial Rate*</th>
                <th class="text-right p-3">Non-Profit Rate*</th>
                <th class="text-right p-3 rounded-tr-lg">Savings</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-800">Marketing Mail Letter (5-digit auto)</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-gray-600">$0.247</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-green-600 font-semibold">$0.146</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-green-600 font-bold">41%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-gray-50">
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-800">Marketing Mail Flat (5-digit auto)</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-gray-600">$0.558</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-green-600 font-semibold">$0.285</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-green-600 font-bold">49%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-800">Marketing Mail Letter (AADC auto)</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-gray-600">$0.296</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-green-600 font-semibold">$0.174</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-green-600 font-bold">41%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-gray-50">
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-800">Marketing Mail Letter (Mixed AADC)</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-gray-600">$0.347</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-green-600 font-semibold">$0.207</td>
                <td class="text-right p-3 text-green-600 font-bold">40%</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-2">*Rates approximate as of 2025. Actual rates depend on presort level, weight, and volume. Contact us for current pricing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-crst-gold/10 border border-crst-gold/30 rounded-xl p-6 mb-10">
          <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-crst-primary mb-2">Real Savings Example</h4>
          <p class="text-navy-600/80 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            A non-profit sending 5,000 fundraising letters per quarter (20,000 annually) at 5-digit automation rates saves approximately <strong>$2,020 per year</strong> compared to commercial rates. Over five years, that's more than $10,000 back in your budget for programs and services.
          </p>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-display text-crst-primary mb-4">Who Qualifies for Non-Profit Rates?</h3>
        <p class="text-navy-600/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          USPS non-profit mailing authorization is available to organizations that meet specific criteria established by the Domestic Mail Manual (DMM). Eligible organization types include:
        </p>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-8">
          {[
            '501(c)(3) charitable organizations',
            'Religious organizations',
            'Educational institutions',
            'Scientific organizations',
            'Veterans\' organizations',
            'Fraternal organizations',
            'Qualified political committees',
            'Volunteer fire departments',
          ].map((type) => (
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 p-3 bg-crst-light/50 rounded-lg">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-crst-gold shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
              </svg>
              <span class="text-sm text-gray-700">{type}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-display text-crst-primary mb-4">PS Form 3624: The Application</h3>
        <p class="text-navy-600/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          PS Form 3624 (Application to Mail at Nonprofit USPS Marketing Mail Prices) is the official USPS form your organization must complete to receive non-profit mailing authorization. The application is submitted to your local USPS Postmaster along with supporting documentation.
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <div class="bg-navy-50 rounded-xl p-6">
            <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy-800 mb-2">Required Documentation</h4>
            <p class="text-navy-600/80 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Your PS Form 3624 application must include: your IRS determination letter (for 501(c)(3) status), articles of incorporation or charter, a description of your organization's activities and purposes, financial statements showing sources of income, and a sample of the type of mail you intend to send at non-profit rates.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-navy-50 rounded-xl p-6">
            <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy-800 mb-2">Processing Timeline</h4>
            <p class="text-navy-600/80 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              USPS typically processes PS Form 3624 applications within 30–60 days. During this period, USPS reviews your documentation, may request additional information, and issues a written authorization if approved. Cornerstone can prepare and review your application before submission to minimize delays.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-navy-50 rounded-xl p-6">
            <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-navy-800 mb-2">Content Restrictions</h4>
            <p class="text-navy-600/80 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Not all mail qualifies for non-profit rates. The content must further your organization's stated purpose. Items that don't qualify include: cooperative mailings with for-profit entities, mailings primarily designed to sell goods/services, and travel advertising (even for non-profit tours). Cornerstone helps ensure your mail content meets USPS non-profit content standards.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-display text-crst-primary mb-4">How Cornerstone Helps Non-Profits</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3 mb-10">
          {[
            { step: '1', title: 'Application Guidance', desc: 'We walk you through PS Form 3624 and help gather the required documentation.' },
            { step: '2', title: 'Mail Piece Design', desc: 'We design your mailpiece to meet both USPS non-profit content standards and automation requirements.' },
            { step: '3', title: 'List Processing', desc: '' },
            { step: '4', title: 'Presort & Postage', desc: 'We presort your mailing for maximum non-profit postal discounts and handle all postage payment.' },
            { step: '5', title: 'Annual Maintenance', desc: 'We help you maintain your authorization and ensure each mailing continues to meet USPS requirements.' },
          ].map((item) => (
            <div class="flex gap-4 p-4 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
              <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-crst-primary text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold shrink-0">{item.step}</div>
              <div>
                <div class="font-heading font-bold text-gray-800 text-sm">{item.title}</div>
                <div class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">
                  {item.step === '3' ? (
                    <>We process your donor/member list through CASS/DPV and NCOA to ensure deliverability and presort accuracy. Keeping your list current through regular <a href="/direct-mail-tools/address-change/" class="text-crst-primary underline hover:text-crst-gold">address change processing</a> is the single biggest factor in mailing ROI.</>
                  ) : item.desc}
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-display text-crst-primary mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
        <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
          <details class="group bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg" open>
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-5 cursor-pointer hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors rounded-lg">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 text-sm pr-4">What is PS Form 3624?</h4>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-400 shrink-0 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" /></svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-100 pt-4">
              PS Form 3624 is the USPS application form that non-profit organizations must submit to qualify for discounted non-profit mailing rates. It requires documentation of your tax-exempt status, organizational purpose, and the type of mail you plan to send.
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="group bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-5 cursor-pointer hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors rounded-lg">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 text-sm pr-4">How much can our non-profit save on postage?</h4>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-400 shrink-0 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" /></svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-100 pt-4">
              Qualifying non-profits typically save 40–60% compared to standard commercial mailing rates. A non-profit sending 5,000 letters quarterly could save over $2,000 annually in postage alone.
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="group bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-5 cursor-pointer hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors rounded-lg">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 text-sm pr-4">Do we need our own mailing permit?</h4>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-400 shrink-0 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" /></svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-100 pt-4">
              Yes. Unlike commercial mailings where Cornerstone can mail under our permit, USPS non-profit authorization must be tied to the non-profit organization's own <a href="/direct-mail-tools/cornerstone-mailing-permits/" class="text-crst-primary underline hover:text-crst-gold">mailing permit</a>. We'll help you set up a permit and apply for non-profit authorization.
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="group bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-5 cursor-pointer hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors rounded-lg">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 text-sm pr-4">Can we send fundraising appeals at non-profit rates?</h4>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-400 shrink-0 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" /></svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-100 pt-4">
              Yes. Fundraising solicitations are one of the most common uses of non-profit mailing rates. As long as the appeal furthers your organization's stated charitable purpose, it qualifies. Annual appeals, capital campaigns, and membership renewals all typically qualify.
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-crst-primary/5 border border-crst-primary/20 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-crst-primary mb-2">Ready to Apply for Non-Profit Rates?</h4>
          <p class="text-navy-600/80 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Contact us for a free consultation. We'll review your organization's eligibility, estimate your postage savings, and guide you through the PS Form 3624 application process.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <a href="/estimate/" class="btn-primary text-sm">Get a Free Estimate</a>
            <a href="/services/non-profit-mailing/" class="btn-secondary text-sm">Non-Profit Mailing Services →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CTASection />
</BaseLayout>
